"caption": "A close-up view looks down into a white bowl holding a pool of yellow liquid arranged as an open, U-shaped ring. A paler, foamy, partly solidified mass fills the upper arc. Thinner liquid spreads toward the lower edge. For the first stretch the bowl and its contents sit undisturbed, with no tool present. Then a metal knife blade, its serrated edge catching the light, enters from the lower right. It presses its tip into the foamy mass and is drawn back and forth across the pool, its insertion point shifting from the right side to the center and then to the left. As it passes, the pale mass and surrounding liquid are locally displaced and deformed, pushed aside and dragged along the surface. The ring outline persists, and the blade's angle and contact point change frame to frame, marking continuous manual sweeping. The sweeping motion carries on through the final frames. The blade remains in contact with the pool, and the displaced mass continues to settle around it.",
